amentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Nick LaLota (R) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term-plus incumbent Nick LaLota seeks a third term in a Long Island district that leans Republican by about four points. He has raised $4.4 million and holds a wide cash advantage over Democrat Chris Gallant, a county legislator who has raised about $1.6 million. Expert raters mostly call the race Likely Republican, with a few at Lean Republican or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a 15 percent chance.\n\nThe only public poll is a Democratic-sponsored survey from December 2025 showing a narrow 3-point race, which is old and of uncertain quality. Headlines have focused on a leaked-images story around Gallant and the absence of debates. The forecast expects LaLota to win by a modest but comfortable margin, with meaningful uncertainty given the lack of fresh polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1953, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.158, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1553, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.188, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1399, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0851, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1487, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1542, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1035, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1186, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1205, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.124, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1216, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1197, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1405, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1018, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.1226, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0863, "margin": -8.0}, {"date